<title>FRANCE: Dupont-Denant downgrades Elf, Total.</title>
<headline>Dupont-Denant downgrades Elf, Total.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brokerage Dupont Denant on Wednesday downgraded Elf and Total because of lower oil prices, fund managers said.</p>
<p>Dupont went to underperformer (note 3) from buy (note 1) for Total and withdrew it from its list of recommendations. For Elf, it changed to neutral (note 2) from buy (1).</p>
<p>Dupont also lowered its forecast for the oil price in 1996/97 to $16.5 from $18.</p>
<p>It said Total's share price fully valued the company and that margins for productivity gains were now limited. At Elf, such gains were still possible.</p>
<p>At 1050, Elf was up 1.11 percent at 545 francs and Total was 0.39 percent higher at 468.80 francs.</p>
</text>
